293
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:05,360
Your ticket carries a facility charge.

294
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:08,170
The airlines pay rent and landing fees.

295
00:10:08,170 --> 00:10:09,828
Your car pays for parking,

296
00:10:09,828 --> 00:10:11,860
rentals or a pickup.

297
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:14,372
The terminal collects from every shop and

298
00:10:14,372 --> 00:10:15,810
every screen.

299
00:10:15,810 --> 00:10:18,340
And federal grants fill in the rest.

300
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:19,134
Five streams,

301
00:10:19,134 --> 00:10:22,470
all flowing into one public owner.

302
00:10:22,717 --> 00:10:26,025
So why do America's airports make money

303
00:10:26,025 --> 00:10:27,727
before you fly?

304
00:10:27,957 --> 00:10:29,773
Because an airport is not just a

305
00:10:29,773 --> 00:10:30,777
runway.

306
00:10:30,887 --> 00:10:32,107
It is a landlord,

307
00:10:32,107 --> 00:10:33,742
a parking operator,

308
00:10:33,742 --> 00:10:35,996
a shopping mall and a toll collector,

309
00:10:35,996 --> 00:10:37,217
all at once.

310
00:10:37,367 --> 00:10:40,264
And every one of those businesses gets

311
00:10:40,264 --> 00:10:42,196
paid long before your wheels leave the

312
00:10:42,196 --> 00:10:43,037
ground.

313
00:10:43,277 --> 00:10:44,795
So next time you land,

314
00:10:44,795 --> 00:10:45,947
look around.

315
00:10:45,947 --> 00:10:46,864
The garage,

316
00:10:46,864 --> 00:10:48,250
the rental counter,

317
00:10:48,250 --> 00:10:49,402
the coffee shop,

318
00:10:49,402 --> 00:10:51,177
the screens on the wall.

319
00:10:51,247 --> 00:10:53,050
Each one is part of how the

320
00:10:53,050 --> 00:10:54,569
airport pays its bills,

321
00:10:54,569 --> 00:10:57,744
long before anyone checks a boarding pass.

322
00:10:57,983 --> 00:11:00,402
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

323
00:11:00,402 --> 00:11:03,287
we follow the money behind another hidden

324
00:11:03,287 --> 00:11:05,663
link of the world economy.

325
00:11:05,883 --> 00:11:08,283
This is The Hidden Economics.
